	(text "# LORA SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (LORA BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet - COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe LoRa subsystem provides long-range Sub-GHz wireless communication using an SX1262 transceiver. \nIt features an integrated LC power-amplifier bias feed, a Johanson matched balun, a PE4259 RF switch for Tx/Rx path multiplexing, \nand a coaxial antenna interface (J12). Communication and control are handled over the shared SPI bus and dedicated control signals \nconnected to the ESP32-S3.\n\n1. TRANSCEIVER CORE AND POWER MANAGEMENT (U16 SX1262IMLTRT)\n* Core Transceiver: U16 (SX1262IMLTRT Sub-GHz LoRa/FSK transceiver).\n* Primary Supply Filtering: Main +3.3V rail filetered by FB1 to produce clear 3V3_RF Rails decoupled \n  by C50 (100nF), C33 (10µF) and bulk C37 (47µF).\n* Core Voltage Rails: All the power pins, powered directly onto 3V3_RF rails (VDD_IN, VBAT, VBAT_IO)\n  ; VREG pin (pin 7) decoupled by C36 (470nF); VR_PA pin (pin 24) decoupled by C39 (100nF) to GND.\n* DC-DC Converter: Internal switching converter DCC_SW pin (pin 9) connected to L3 (15µH power inductor) for high-efficiency power regulation.\n* Reference Clock: Y1 (32MHz crystal unit) connected across XTA (pin 1) and XTB (pin 2).\n\n2. RF FRONT-END, BALUN, AND ANTENNA PATH\n* Power-Amp Bias Feed: RFO_TX pin (pin 23) powered via L4 (27nH RF choke inductor) connected to the VR_PA rail.\n* Integrated Balun (FL2 0900FM15K0039): Converts differential RF_N (pin 22) and RF_P (pin 21) transceiver lines into \n  a single-ended signal. Output passes through C44 (47pF) to generate the RF2_PATH (Rx) signal.\n* Transmit Path: RFO_TX output routes through C40 (47pF) to generate the RF1_PATH (Tx) signal.\n* RF Switch (U15 PE4259): Multiplexes Tx and Rx paths to the antenna. RF1_PATH connects to pin 1, RF2_PATH connects to pin 3, \n  and CTRL (pin 4) is driven by the DIO2 line from the SX1262. Pin 5 (RFC) outputs the combined ANT signal.\n* Antenna Interface: Single-ended ANT line routes through DC-blocking capacitor C38 (47pF) to coaxial connector J12.\n\n3. CONTROL LOGIC AND SPI BUS INTERFACE\n* Shared SPI Bus: Communicates via SPI.SPI_SCK (pin 18), SPI.SPI_MISO (pin 16), and SPI.SPI_MOSI (pin 17).\n* Chip Select Isolation: SPI.SPI_NSS pin (pin 19) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R47 (10kΩ) resistor to ensure proper bus selection.\n* Hardware Reset: Active-LOW RESET pin (pin 15) tied to RESET_LoRa net from ESP32-S3 (IO7).\n* Busy & Interrupt Lines: BUSY pin (pin 14) outputs BUSY_LoRa status to ESP32-S3 (IO10). DIO1 pin (pin 13) \n  outputs DIO1 interrupts to ESP32-S3 (IO11).\n* Switch Control: DIO2 pin (pin 12) directly drives the PE4259 CTRL pin for automatic Tx/Rx path switching.\n\n4. SUBSYSTEM INTERFACE MATRIX\nSPI.SPI_NSS: Active-LOW chip select line (Pulled HIGH via R47).\nSPI.SPI_SCK / MISO / MOSI: Shared hardware SPI bus lines connected to ESP32-S3.\nRESET_LoRa: Transceiver hardware reset line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO7).\nBUSY_LoRa: Transceiver busy status line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO10).\nDIO1: Interrupt request signal line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO11).\nJ12: Coaxial antenna connector for external Sub-GHz antenna."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
